# Wireframe: Issue Detail Page — Labels Section

## Changelog

| Version | Type | Description |
|---------|------|-------------|
| 1.1.0 | MINOR | Added IssueFormModal labels field wireframe; added LabelPicker loading state; pinned labels-section aria-label value |

## Purpose & Flow Context

Users view, attach, and detach labels on an issue without leaving the detail page or saving the full issue form. Entry: issue list row click or direct URL to `/issues/:id`. Exit: Back to issue list, or labels updated in place.

---

## Notation Legend

| Symbol | Meaning | Symbol | Meaning |
|--------|---------|--------|---------|
| `[...]` | Button / interactive element | `[>...▼]` | Dropdown |
| `_______` | Text input / editable field | `[X]` | Close / dismiss |
| `⏳` | Loading / skeleton | `⚠` | Error state |
| `#` | Heading level indicator | `●` | Label badge (colored pill) |
| `[+ ...]` | Add action trigger | `[✓]` | Checked option |

## Accessibility — Shared Conventions

All interactive screens inherit these.

| Concern | Convention |
|---------|------------|
| Landmarks | `header`, `main`, `contentinfo` |
| Heading order | One `h1` per screen, `h2` for sections |
| Accessible names | Icon-only controls get `aria-label` |
| Keyboard | Tab, Enter/Space, Escape, Arrow keys |
| Target size | ≥24×24 CSS px reservation |
| Non-color intent | Icon + text, never color alone |

---

## Layout Regions

**Grid**: Single-column layout within the shared app-shell. Spacing cadence: 8px rhythm.

**App-shell**: Shared header (logo, nav, user menu) + max-width container.

| Region | Content | Notes |
|--------|---------|-------|
| Header | Back button, breadcrumb | Sticky top |
| Issue metadata | Identifier, title, status badge, priority, dates, assignee | Top of main content |
| Labels section | LabelList component | Between metadata and description |
| Description | Issue body text | Below labels |
| Actions | Edit, Delete buttons | Below description |
| Watchers | WatcherSection | Below actions |
| Comments | CommentList with divider | Bottom of page |

**Content hierarchy** (by visual priority):
1. Issue identifier + title (identifies the entity)
2. Status / priority / assignee metadata (quick triage context)
3. Labels section (manageable tags)
4. Description (details)
5. Action buttons
6. Watchers, comments

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  [← Back]                                                        |
|                                                                   |
|  #ABC-123                                                        |
|  # Issue Title Here                                              |
|                                                                   |
|  [Todo ▼]  Urgent  |  Assignee: John  |  Created: Jul 22 2026    |
|                                                                   |
|  +-- Labels ---------------------------------------------------+ |
|  |  ● bug  [X]   ● frontend  [X]   ● high-priority  [X]      | |
|  |  [+ Add label]                                              | |
|  +-------------------------------------------------------------+ |
|                                                                   |
|  ## Description                                                  |
|  Issue description text here...                                  |
|                                                                   |
|  [Edit]  [Delete]                                                 |
|                                                                   |
|  ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────   |
|                                                                   |
|  WatcherSection                                                   |
|                                                                   |
|  CommentList                                                      |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

## Components & Affordances

| Element | DS Component | Behavior | Edge Cases |
|---------|-------------|----------|------------|
| `[← Back]` | `Button` (ghost) | Navigates to `/issues` | — |
| `[Todo ▼]` | `IssueStatusBadge` | Dropdown to change status; fires `onStatusChange` | Loading state during API call |
| Priority label | `span` (colored text) | Static display | Uses priority color tokens |
| `● bug [X]` | `LabelBadge` (removable) | Pill badge; `[X]` fires `onDetach(labelId)` | Truncate long names with ellipsis |
| `[+ Add label]` | `Button` (ghost) | Opens `LabelPicker` popover | Disabled during attach API call |
| `[Edit]` | `Button` (secondary) | Opens edit modal | — |
| `[Delete]` | `Button` (danger) | Opens confirm dialog | — |

## Data Display

Labels display as a horizontal wrapped flex list of pill badges. Each badge: rounded-full, primary-tinted background, label name text, optional X icon for removal. No sort/pagination — all labels fit inline. Long label names truncate with text-ellipsis.

## Content & Microcopy Intent

| Slot | Intent | Notes |
|------|--------|-------|
| Labels section heading | Section label: "Labels" | Visible as section label |
| `● {name}` | Label name — human-readable, same as the backend label definition name | Consistent with label picker |
| `[X]` on badge | "Remove {label name} label" — accessible name | Icon-only, needs `aria-label` |
| `[+ Add label]` | "Attach a new label to this issue" | Consistent action label |
| Empty state text | "No labels" | Concise; followed by Add label CTA |
| Error message | "Failed to load labels. [Retry]" | Actionable error |

## States

### Populated (Default)

Labels section shows 1+ `LabelBadge` items in a flex-wrap row, each with a remove button. "[+ Add label]" button visible at end of row or on its own line.

```
  ● bug  [X]   ● frontend  [X]   ● high-priority  [X]   [+ Add label]
```

### Empty

No labels attached. "[+ Add label]" button is the primary CTA.

```
  No labels    [+ Add label]
```

### Loading

Two skeleton pill shapes matching the dimensions of `LabelBadge` components. No "Add label" button until loaded.

```
  ⏳──────────   ⏳────────────   ⏳────────
  (skeleton pill)  (skeleton pill)  (skeleton pill)
```

### Error

`ErrorBanner` inline within the labels section, below the issue metadata line. Retry button re-fetches labels.

```
  +-- ⚠ --------------------------------------------------------+
  |  Failed to load labels. Please try again.    [Retry]         |
  +--------------------------------------------------------------+
```

### Success / Confirmation

Label attach/detach are optimistic — no explicit success state. On API failure, toast appears with "Failed to attach/detach label" and the optimistic change is rolled back.

## Responsive

| Breakpoint | Changes |
|------------|---------|
| Desktop (>1024px) | Full layout as described |
| Tablet (768-1024px) | Same layout; labels wrap naturally |
| Mobile (<768px) | Full-width content; labels wrap; touch targets remain ≥24×24px |

## Accessibility — Screen Composition

| Concern | Implementation |
|---------|----------------|
| Landmarks | `header` for back button + metadata, `main` for issue content including labels section |
| Heading order | `h1` for issue title, `h2` for "Description", labels section is region without heading (`aria-label="Issue labels"`) |
| Reading / Focus order | Back → title → status badge → labels list → add label → description → actions |
| Accessible names | Remove button: `aria-label="Remove {label name} label"`; Add label: `aria-label="Add label to issue"` |
| Keyboard operability | Tab through label badges; Enter/Space on remove button to detach; Tab to "Add label" to open picker |
| Target size | ≥24×24 CSS px on all badge remove buttons and action buttons |
| Focus not obscured | No sticky regions above labels; focus scrolls naturally |
| Non-color intent | Label badges use text + color; remove icon has accessible name |

*Defer to design-system: pixel contrast, focus-appearance, per-component target-size/keyboard.*

---

# Wireframe: Label Picker Popover

## Purpose & Flow Context

Inline popover to browse, search, and select available label definitions to attach to the current issue. Entry: clicking "[+ Add label]" on IssueDetailPage. Exit: selecting a label (attaches + closes) or clicking outside / pressing Escape (closes without action).

## Layout Regions

**Grid**: Overlay popover, no grid. Absolute-positioned below the trigger button.

**No app-shell** (popover is not a page).

| Region | Content | Notes |
|--------|---------|-------|
| Search field | TextInput with placeholder "Search labels..." | Filters list as user types |
| Label list | Scrollable list of checkable rows | Max-height: 240px, overflow-y scroll |
| Empty state | "No labels found" | When search yields no results |

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  [ Search labels..._____________________________ ]               |
|  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────               |
|  [✓] Bug              ●                                             |
|  [ ] Frontend         ●                                             |
|  [✓] High Priority    ●                                             |
|  [ ] Enhancement      ●                                             |
|  [ ] Documentation    ●                                             |
|  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────               |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

## Components & Affordances

| Element | DS Component | Behavior | Edge Cases |
|---------|-------------|----------|------------|
| Search input | `TextInput` | Filters label list on input; autofocus on open | Clear button when text entered |
| Label row | `div[role="option"]` | Click toggles selection; Arrow keys navigate | Selected row shows checkmark |
| Checkbox | `Checkbox` | Visual selected/unselected state | — |
| Label color dot | `span` | Colored circle indicator | Matches label definition color |

## Data Display

Filterable list. Each row shows a colored dot (matching label definition color), label name, and checkbox indicator. No columns/sort/pagination — all available labels in a scrollable list.

## Content & Microcopy Intent

| Slot | Intent | Notes |
|------|--------|-------|
| Search placeholder | "Search labels..." | Instructs user to type to filter |
| Label row text | Label definition name | Human-readable, consistent with badge display |
| Empty search state | "No labels found" | No labels match the search query |
| No labels available | "No labels available" | No label definitions exist in workspace |

## States

### Open — Populated

Search input focused. List shows all available labels. Already-attached labels show checked with `✓`.

### Open — Filtered

Search input has text. List filtered to matching label names. Matching term highlighted if applicable.

### Open — Empty (no results)

Search yielded no matches. Shows "No labels found" message with no CTA (user must modify search or close).

### Open — Empty (no label definitions)

No label definitions exist in the workspace. Shows "No labels available" message.

### Closed (trigger state)

"[+ Add label]" ghost button visible in the LabelList section on IssueDetailPage.

### Open — Loading

Available label definitions are being fetched asynchronously. Popover shows a disabled search input and skeleton option rows matching the expected list layout. If zero label definitions exist after fetch, transitions to "Open — Empty (no label definitions)".

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  ⏳ [ Search labels..._____________________________ ]  (disabled) |
|  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────               |
|  ⏳ [ ] ●─────────────                                             |
|  ⏳ [ ] ●─────────────                                             |
|  ⏳ [ ] ●─────────────                                             |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

## Responsive

| Breakpoint | Changes |
|------------|---------|
| Desktop | Popover positioned below trigger, left-aligned, min-width 240px |
| Mobile (<768px) | Full-width popover within the content area; positioned below trigger |

## Accessibility — Screen Composition

| Concern | Implementation |
|---------|----------------|
| Landmarks | Popover is a `dialog` with `role="dialog"` and `aria-label="Select a label"` |
| Heading order | No headings — popover is not a page section |
| Reading / Focus order | Focus trapped inside popover on open; first focusable element = search input |
| Accessible names | Search input: `aria-label="Search labels"`; each option: `aria-label="{label name}"`; close: no close button (Escape to close) |
| Keyboard operability | Arrow Up/Down navigate options; Enter/Space selects focused option; Escape closes; Tab cycles within popover |
| Target size | ≥24×24 CSS px on each option row |
| Focus not obscured | Popover overlays content; backdrop click or Escape closes |
| Non-color intent | Label rows use checkbox indicator + name text; color dots are decorative |

*Defer to design-system: pixel contrast, focus-appearance, per-component target-size/keyboard.*

---

# Wireframe: Issue Form — Labels Field

## Purpose & Flow Context

Labels multi-select field within the create/edit issue form modal. Entry: "New Issue" button on IssuesList (create) or "Edit" button on IssueDetailPage (edit). Exit: form submitted (labels sent as `labelIds: string[]`) or cancelled (selections discarded).

## Layout Regions

**Grid**: Within the existing IssueFormModal layout — no separate grid. Labels field is a section in the form body, between description and priority/metadata fields.

**No app-shell** (form modal is an overlay, not a page).

| Region | Content | Notes |
|--------|---------|-------|
| Form body | Title, description, labels multi-select, priority, assignee, dates | Scrollable within modal |
| Labels field | `Select` (multi-select variant) | Dropdown with search + removable selected tags |

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  [Create Issue]                                                    |
|  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────             |
|  Title:  [______________________________________]                  |
|                                                                     |
|  Description:                                                      |
|  [_________________________________________________________]       |
|  [_________________________________________________________]       |
|                                                                     |
|  Labels:  [Select or type to search... ▼]                          |
|           ● bug [X]  ● frontend [X]                                |
|                                                                     |
|  Priority:  [Medium ▼]                                             |
|  Assignee:  [Select assignee ▼]                                    |
|                                                                     |
|  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────             |
|  [Cancel]                              [Create Issue (primary)]    |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

## Components & Affordances

| Element | DS Component | Behavior | Edge Cases |
|---------|-------------|----------|------------|
| Labels multi-select | `Select` (multi-select variant) | Dropdown with search; selected labels shown as removable tag pills within the field container; `labelIds: string[]` submitted on save | No label definitions → show "No labels available" disabled state |
| Label tag inside select | Tag (inline within Select) | Each selected label shown as small pill with remove (X) to deselect | Truncate long names with ellipsis |
| `[Create Issue]` / `[Save Changes]` | `Button` (primary) | Submits form with `labelIds` in payload | Disabled while submitting; label validation error blocks submit |
| `[Cancel]` | `Button` (ghost) | Closes modal, discards label selections | — |

## Data Display

Multi-select dropdown. Typing filters available label definitions. Selected labels render as removable tag pills inside the field container. No sort/pagination — all available labels fit in the dropdown list. The dropdown uses a checkmark indicator for selected state.

## Content & Microcopy Intent

| Slot | Intent | Notes |
|------|--------|-------|
| Labels field label | "Labels" | Persistent label above the multi-select field |
| Search placeholder | "Select or type to search..." | Instructs user to browse or type to filter |
| Selected tag remove | "Remove {label name}" | Accessible name for each tag's X button |
| No labels available | "No labels available" | When zero label definitions exist in the workspace |
| Submit (create) | "Create Issue" | Primary action — creates the issue with selected labels |
| Submit (edit) | "Save Changes" | Primary action — saves issue with updated labels |

## States

### Create

Labels multi-select empty. All available label definitions listed for selection. None pre-selected.

### Edit (pre-selected)

Labels multi-select shows current issue labels as pre-selected tag pills. User can add additional labels or remove existing ones before saving.

### Submitting

Form shows loading state on submit button. Labels field and all form controls disabled during submission.

### Validation Error

Server-side error for `labelIds` displays inline below the field: "One or more selected labels are invalid." Field border turns danger color.

## Responsive

| Breakpoint | Changes |
|------------|---------|
| Desktop | Centered overlay modal; multi-select inline with 240px min-width |
| Mobile (<768px) | Full-screen modal; multi-select full-width; touch targets ≥24×24px |

## Accessibility — Screen Composition

| Concern | Implementation |
|---------|----------------|
| Landmarks | Modal uses `role="dialog"` with `aria-label="Create issue"` or `aria-label="Edit issue"` |
| Heading order | Modal title is `h2` within the dialog |
| Reading / Focus order | Focus trapped inside modal on open; first focusable = title input |
| Accessible names | Search input inside multi-select: `aria-label="Search labels"`; remove tag: `aria-label="Remove {name} label"` |
| Keyboard operability | Tab through fields; Arrow keys navigate multi-select options; Enter/Space to toggle selection; Escape closes modal |
| Target size | ≥24×24 CSS px on all interactive elements |
| Focus not obscured | Modal overlay prevents focus behind it; backdrop-inert active |
| Non-color intent | Selected vs unselected states use checkmark icon + name text, not color alone |

*Defer to design-system: pixel contrast, focus-appearance, per-component target-size/keyboard.*